---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

// Facts on this page come from official Blizzard sources: the announcement
// and Deep Dive recaps on news.blizzard.com and the CN official site
// (wow.blizzard.cn). Community/transcribed content links out to the
// calculator and Legacy pages instead of duplicating their caveats.
const verified = 'September 16, 2026';

const dates = [
  {
    region: 'Global — Beta',
    date: '2026-09-17',
    label: 'September 17, 2026',
    note: 'Beta opens worldwide; first look at live talent data.',
  },
  {
    region: 'China — Beta (国服 Beta)',
    date: '2026-10-06',
    label: 'October 6, 2026',
    note: 'CN beta via the Heavenly Epic pack (天裔史诗礼包) pre-purchase.',
  },
  {
    region: 'Global — Launch',
    date: '2026-11-04',
    label: 'November 4, 2026',
    note: 'World of Warcraft: Forever launches in the Americas, Europe, and Korea.',
  },
  {
    region: 'China — Launch (国服上线)',
    date: '2026-11-05',
    label: 'November 5, 2026',
    note: 'Global simultaneous launch day for the CN realm (全球同步上线).',
  },
];

const classes = [
  { id: 'warrior', name: 'Warrior', trees: 'Arms / Fury / Protection' },
  { id: 'paladin', name: 'Paladin', trees: 'Holy / Protection / Retribution' },
  { id: 'hunter', name: 'Hunter', trees: 'Beast Mastery / Marksmanship / Survival' },
  { id: 'rogue', name: 'Rogue', trees: 'Assassination / Combat / Subtlety' },
  { id: 'priest', name: 'Priest', trees: 'Discipline / Holy / Shadow' },
  { id: 'shaman', name: 'Shaman', trees: 'Elemental / Enhancement / Restoration' },
  { id: 'mage', name: 'Mage', trees: 'Arcane / Fire / Frost' },
  { id: 'warlock', name: 'Warlock', trees: 'Affliction / Demonology / Destruction' },
  { id: 'druid', name: 'Druid', trees: 'Balance / Feral / Restoration' },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="WoW Forever Wiki — World of Warcraft: Forever Explained 魔兽世界无限"
  description="What is World of Warcraft: Forever? Official launch dates, talent and Legacy systems, camping, professions, rulesets, and the nine classes — the WoW Forever wiki."
  breadcrumbs={[
    { name: 'Home', url: '/' },
    { name: 'Wiki', url: '/wiki/' },
  ]}
>
  <section class="page-head">
    <h1>WoW Forever Wiki</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      World of Warcraft: Forever — known in China as
      <span lang="zh-Hans">《魔兽世界》：“无限”</span> — is Blizzard's new
      standalone World of Warcraft game set in a reimagined original Azeroth,
      built around the classic 1–60 journey and expanded with modern systems.
      This wiki collects the official facts today and will grow into full
      class and leveling guides as the beta data settles.
    </p>
    <p>
      <span class="stage-badge">
        Official sources · facts verified <time datetime="2026-09-16">{verified}</time>
      </span>
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="page-section" aria-labelledby="wiki-overview">
    <h2 id="wiki-overview">What Is World of Warcraft: Forever?</h2>
    <div class="panel" style="margin: var(--space-4) 0; overflow: hidden; padding: 0;">
      <img
        src="/images/hero-forever.jpg"
        alt="Official World of Warcraft: Forever key art — an adventurer and their bear companion overlooking a river valley in Azeroth"
        width="1920"
        height="1080"
        style="display: block; width: 100%; height: auto;"
        loading="lazy"
      />
    </div>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        Announced at BlizzCon 2026, Forever returns to the original Azeroth —
        the world before the Burning Crusade — and treats it as a living,
        long-term world rather than a legacy server. Blizzard positions it
        alongside Modern and Classic as a third way to play World of
        Warcraft: the familiar 1–60 journey, rebuilt and continuously
        expanded. The CN tagline is
        <span lang="zh-Hans">“回应崭新天地的召唤”</span> — “answer the call
        of a brand-new world.”
      </p>
      <p>
        Combat keeps the deliberate, tactical pacing of Classic — solo pulls
        take roughly 10–15 seconds, crowd control matters, and threat is
        real — while itemization, talents, and account-wide progression add
        new decisions on top.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="page-section" aria-labelledby="wiki-dates">
    <h2 id="wiki-dates">WoW Forever Beta &amp; Launch Dates</h2>
    <div class="table-scroll">
      <table class="data-table">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th scope="col">Region</th>
            <th scope="col">Date</th>
            <th scope="col">Notes</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {
            dates.map((d) => (
              <tr>
                <th scope="row">{d.region}</th>
                <td>
                  <time datetime={d.date}>{d.label}</time>
                </td>
                <td>{d.note}</td>
              </tr>
            ))
          }
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="prose talent-meta">
      Dates come from the official announcement and the CN official site;
      exact hours were not stated consistently (PST/PDT markers differ
      between paragraphs), so this wiki does not publish a countdown.
      Re-verify with official channels closer to launch.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="page-section" aria-labelledby="wiki-talents">
    <h2 id="wiki-talents">The WoW Forever Talent System</h2>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        Forever keeps the classic talent structure — three trees per class,
        one point per level from level 10, rows unlocking every 5 points —
        but the nodes themselves change: a new keystone tier arrives at the
        16-point mark alongside the classic 11/21/31 milestones, some 1.12
        talents are kept or reworked, and several iconic buffs that used to
        be talents become baseline abilities.
      </p>
      <p>
        Start planning in the
        <a href="/">free talent calculator</a> (all nine classes, shareable
        builds), or see
        <a href="/changes/">what changed vs. Classic</a> talent by talent.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="page-section" aria-labelledby="wiki-legacy">
    <h2 id="wiki-legacy">The WoW Forever Legacy System <span lang="zh-Hans">（传承系统）</span></h2>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        Legacy is Forever's account-wide progression layer: you earn Legacy
        Points by completing Legacy Challenges, and each character spends
        them in three non-combat trees — <strong>Adventure</strong>,
        <strong>Resourcefulness</strong>, and <strong>Professions</strong>.
        At launch each character can spend up to 16 points, with 65 earnable
        at the start; points beyond the cap feed a cosmetic reward track.
        Hardcore keeps its own separate Legacy ecosystem.
      </p>
      <p>
        Browse every perk in the
        <a href="/legacy/">Legacy system reference &amp; planner</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="page-section" aria-labelledby="wiki-world">
    <h2 id="wiki-world">World &amp; Systems</h2>
    <div class="card-grid">
      <div class="panel">
        <h3>Camping <span lang="zh-Hans">（营地）</span></h3>
        <p class="talent-meta">
          The Cooking Fire becomes a place to rest: campsites grant one-hour
          buffs, vendors, repairs, and profession workstations. Every
          profession can craft camp objects — Blacksmiths place Sharpening
          Wheels, Tailors raise Faction Banners, Herbalists light Incense
          Candles.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="panel">
        <h3>Professions <span lang="zh-Hans">（专业）</span></h3>
        <p class="talent-meta">
          600+ new recipes across all professions and level ranges, crafted
          food with experience bonuses and stat boosts, and advanced
          Blueprint recipes that drop from specific dungeon bosses.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="panel">
        <h3>Realmless Azeroth <span lang="zh-Hans">（无服务器世界）</span></h3>
        <p class="talent-meta">
          No realm list: you pick a ruleset — Normal, PvP, Roleplaying, or
          Hardcore (after launch) — and group within it. Characters use
          two-part names unique per region, and factions remain separate.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="panel">
        <h3>Transmogrification <span lang="zh-Hans">（幻化）</span></h3>
        <p class="talent-meta">
          New to original Azeroth, with an opt-out: players who prefer the
          untouched look can disable seeing transmog entirely. Dungeon
          appearances are granted to all eligible looters; epic raid drops
          keep their prestige.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="panel">
        <h3>Combat &amp; Itemization</h3>
        <p class="talent-meta">
          Spell/melee/ranged hit combine into one stat, as do the three
          critical chances — a buff for hybrids. New affixes reduce parry/
          dodge against you, caster weapons gain spell power, and trinkets
          get situational environment- and creature-type effects.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="panel">
        <h3>Mounts &amp; Riding</h3>
        <p class="talent-meta">
          Forever adopts the Burning Crusade-style cost model: the up-front
          mount cost moves into riding training, and learning the skill
          grants a mount.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="page-section" aria-labelledby="wiki-classes">
    <h2 id="wiki-classes">The Nine Classes in WoW Forever</h2>
    <p class="prose">
      Forever launches with the nine classic classes, three talent trees
      each — plan any of them in the calculator:
    </p>
    <ul class="class-grid">
      {
        classes.map((c) => (
          <li>
            <a class="class-card" href={`/${c.id}/`}>
              <img
                src={`/icons/classes/class_${c.id}.jpg`}
                alt=""
                width="56"
                height="56"
                class="class-icon"
                loading="lazy"
              />
              <span>
                <span class="class-name">{c.name}</span>
                <span class="class-trees">{c.trees}</span>
              </span>
            </a>
          </li>
        ))
      }
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="page-section" aria-labelledby="wiki-guides">
    <h2 id="wiki-guides">Guides — Coming With Beta Data</h2>
    <p class="prose">
      This wiki is the foundation for the site's guide section. Once the
      beta client lands on September 17 and the numbers stop moving, each
      anchor above becomes a full guide hub: leveling paths, per-spec build
      orders, and Legacy challenge routes. Tools that already work today:
    </p>
    <ol class="steps">
      <li>
        <h3>Talent calculator</h3>
        <p>
          Plan and share 51-point builds for all nine classes —
          <a href="/">start here</a>.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>Legacy planner</h3>
        <p>
          Spread each character's 16 launch Legacy points —
          <a href="/legacy/">plan your spread</a>.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>Build compare</h3>
        <p>
          Diff two setups point by point — <a href="/compare/">open compare</a>.
        </p>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section class="page-section" aria-labelledby="wiki-sources">
    <h2 id="wiki-sources">Sources</h2>
    <p class="prose">
      Facts on this page come from official Blizzard channels: the
      <a
        href="https://news.blizzard.com/en-us/article/24302093/carve-a-new-path-with-world-of-warcraft-forever"
        rel="external"
      >announcement</a>
      and
      <a
        href="https://news.blizzard.com/en-us/article/24303313/world-of-warcraft-forever-deep-dive-panel-recap"
        rel="external"
      >Deep Dive panel recap</a>
      on news.blizzard.com, and the
      <a href="https://wow.blizzard.cn/forever/" rel="external"
        >CN official site</a
      >
      for CN beta and launch dates. Key art is Blizzard Entertainment's,
      used on this fan-made site to identify the game (see
      <a href="/about/">About</a>). Talent and Legacy perk data — which is
      transcribed from demo footage rather than official text — follows the
      separate <a href="/sources/">data &amp; sources policy</a>.
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
